WATCH OUT

  - Software reaches the workstation only through a recorded
    tamlinux-packages assembly and tam-deploy, never from a checkout.
  - Boot, login, disk, firmware and package-removal steps run one at a
    time, each approved by Fred, with a rollback point recorded first.
  - desktop/check-all runs the whole suite. Warn Fred before --proofs:
    proofs start real programs that may crash.
  - Agents push only develop and feature branches; test, main, tags and
    releases move on Fred's words.
  - The fred.* plugins under desktop/plugins/ keep their own docs/ai/
    folders: they are archives of the frozen standalone plugin
    repositories, not this repository's records.
  - Development builds use ~/.local/bin and ~/.local/lib; releases
    install to /usr/bin and /usr/lib. Verify release commands by their
    installed system paths.
